    "intro_html":  "Birria is the Jalisco braise that took over every taco menu in America, and the thing most people miss is that the chiles do the work, not the meat. Guajillo, ancho, and arbol get toasted and soaked, then blended into a sauce that chuck roast braises in for hours until it shreds into its own deep red consomme. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
